    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0160" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5301: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-04T18:00:00+08:00">June 4, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 4—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>612. Upon signing of Sino-Japanese agreement at [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >sic</hi>] the Joint Commission consisting of British, American, French and
                    Italian Consuls and British, American, French and Italian Military Attachés was
                    appointed under article 4 of the agreement. Information from Shanghai indicates
                    that main undertakings of Japanese under agreement of May 5 have been completed.
                    Unless the Department desires to the contrary, I am withdrawing Lieutenant Soule
                    who is my present military representative upon the Commission and I shall
                    request Admiral Taylor to designate a marine officer stationed at Shanghai to
                    take his place during remainder of work of Commission.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d68-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d68-f1" n="42" xml:id="d68-f1-content">
                <p>The proposed change was approved by the Department in its telegram No. 144, June
                    6, 3 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
